.\" groff man page for the Basic Next reference tool.
.TH BN 1 "September 6, 2026" "bn 0.4.4" "Basic Next"
.SH NAME
bn \- Basic Next reference checker, interpreter, and compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bn
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.I file.bn
.RI [ "-- program-args" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bn
processes UTF-8 Basic Next source through a source-spanned pipeline:
lexer, parser/AST, semantic analysis, typed BN IR, and either the reference
interpreter or the LLVM backend.
.PP
The executable module must define
.BR "FUNCTION Start" .
No project file is required for a single program.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Validate lexical, syntactic, and semantic rules. With
.BR --emit ,
print a selected frontend artifact.
.TP
.B lex
Print the token stream.
.TP
.B run
Validate, lower to typed BN IR, and execute
.BR Start .
The successful process status is the program result.
.TP
.B build
Lower the supported typed BN IR subset to LLVM IR. Without
.BR -o ,
print LLVM IR. With
.BR -o ,
invoke Clang to create a native executable or Clang and
.B wasm-ld
to create a linked WebAssembly module.
.TP
.B lsp
Serve the Language Server Protocol over standard input and output.
.TP
.B dap
Serve the Debug Adapter Protocol over standard input and output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -v , " --verbose"
Print pipeline stages. Repeat it, or use
.BR -vv ,
to also print tokens.
.TP
.BI --emit " tokens|ast|typed-ast|ir"
Select the frontend artifact printed by
.BR check .
.TP
.BR -o , " --output " file
Write the selected artifact or compiled program to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI --target " native|wasm32"
Select the
.B build
target. The default is
.BR native .
.TP
.BI --opt " none|1|2|3|s"
Select the Clang/WebAssembly linker optimization level. The default is
.BR 2 ;
.B s
optimizes for size.
.TP
.B --no-filesystem
With
.BR run ,
reject a
.B HOST.FileSystem
import before
.BR Start .
The Jupyter kernel uses this boundary.
.TP
.B --trace
Report the interpreter entry point.
.TP
.BI --warnings " errors"
Promote all warning diagnostics to errors.
.TP
.BI --allow " CODE"
Suppress one warning diagnostic (repeatable).
.TP
.BI --warn " CODE"
Keep one warning diagnostic at warning level.
.TP
.BI --deny " CODE"
Promote one warning diagnostic to an error.
.TP
.BI --log-level " error|warn|info|debug"
Process log verbosity during build.
.TP
.BI --log-file " file"
Companion process log file path during build.
.TP
.B --no-log
Disable companion process logging.
.TP
.BI --config " file"
Load warning and process logging configuration from
.IR file .
.TP
.BI --color " auto|always|never"
Control ANSI colour on status messages.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print the tool version.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print command help.
.TP
.B --
End tool options. Remaining values become program arguments.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.B HOST.Args
is available only in the executable module and requires no import.
.B HOST.Args[0]
is the absolute source path under
.BR "bn run" ;
later entries are values after
.BR -- .
.B LEN(HOST.Args)
returns the full count.
.PP
.B HOST.Main ,
.BR SYSTEM ,
.BR ArgumentCount() ,
and
.B Argument(index)
were withdrawn in 0.2.
.SH MODULES
Every import declares an alias. Imported declarations are referenced as
.IR alias.member .
User modules belong beneath
.BR modules/ .
Standard modules such as
.BR BNMath ,
.BR BNData ,
.BR BNLog ,
.BR BNWeb ,
and
.B BNJson
belong beneath
.B modules/bn/
and require explicit imports.
.PP
.B HOST
is the only built-in interface object. Facilities provided include
.BR HOST.Args ,
.BR HOST.Clock ,
.BR HOST.Console ,
.BR HOST.Random ,
.BR HOST.FileSystem ,
and
.BR HOST.Net .
.SH WEBASSEMBLY
A WebAssembly artifact produced by
.B "bn build --target wasm32 -o program.wasm"
runs in the reference Node.js host:
.PP
.nf
.RS
node bin/bn-wasm program.wasm [args...]
.RE
.fi
.PP
The host supplies stream input/output, arguments, allocation, and seeded
random. Filesystem and positioned-console capabilities are unavailable.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
A Basic Next diagnostic exits 1. Invalid command use, missing files, unavailable
toolchains, and unsupported compiler lowering exit 2. Diagnostics include a
stable code and source span when applicable.
.PP
.B BUILD_LOWERING_UNAVAILABLE
means the program is valid but outside the current compiler subset; use
.B bn run
for the reference semantics.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BN_WASM_LD
Command or path used as the WebAssembly linker.
.PP
.B bn
does not read environment variables for language behaviour.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I docs/language/0.4/0.4.ebnf
Highest-priority accepted grammar planning surface.
.TP
.I docs/language/0.4/0.4.md
Active 0.4 language specification draft.
.TP
.I docs/language/0.4/keywords.md
Keyword and reserved-form contract.
.TP
.I docs/project/usage.md
Installation, examples, limits, and troubleshooting.
.TP
.I docs/project/kernel.md
Jupyter host contract.
.SH LIMITATIONS
LLVM lowering covers a typed scalar and vector subset and rejects unsupported IR
explicitly. Time-zone values do not apply TZDB zone rules. The VS Code adapter
is launch-only and has no breakpoints or stepping.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
bn check examples/hello.bn
bn run examples/language-tour.bn
bn run examples/hello.bn -- extra-argument
bn check --emit ir examples/factorial.bn
bn build examples/hello.bn -o hello
bn build --target wasm32 examples/hello.bn -o hello.wasm
.RE
.fi
